  "configuration_id": "config_020",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, PCA, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) is the current best at 0.619 acc, and the single→multi-profile jump (+9.2%) was the largest improvement observed, indicating that how multiple profiles are aggregated is a critical design lever. However, we only have one data point for aggregation (avgpool), so we have no evidence on whether a learned aggregation (transformer) would further improve performance. Question tested: config_020 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding all other settings identical to config_018, giving a clean ablation of aggregation strategy. Why best next experiment: Under a limited budget, resolving whether simple averaging suffices or whether learned cross-profile attention is needed is the highest-uncertainty, highest-impact decision remaining. If transformer helps, it unlocks a new optimization axis across all future multimodal experiments; if it does not, we can confidently fix aggregation at avgpool and redirect budget toward image encoder (ViT-L) or RNA encoder (scvi/scgpt) choices. This minimal-change design maximizes information per experiment."
}

